+# THE COALESCENCE — everything proven in this repository except the continuum gap, sorted by what it is, and the one open link named at its sharpest (Edwin Boston III, 2026-10-30 04:2x EDT, read from `date`)
+
+> Status: a READING of the repository's own pages, records and kernel runs at `main` b5d4b04 (nine commits of the night unpushed) and of the III tree at 0ab9f25fd, written to the operator's order of 2026-10-30 ("find everything there proven except the infinite 4D, and coalesce"). Every row names its discharge site and uses the status word its own page uses. Nothing above β = 0.2452 is claimed. This page is about the lattice theory, its certified radius and the reduction; it is not the continuum gap, and §5 says exactly what stands between the two.
+
+## 1. The chain in one paragraph
+
+THE GROUND reads the Alpöge–Sussman corpus as Theorem 2.1 (what their manuscripts assert: convergence of centred plaquette-energy correlations on each torus, infinite-volume limits along subsequences, Osterwalder–Schrader axioms and a Wightman field in each clustering component, a short-distance law fixing the coupling) and takes the footnote of Proposition 3.2 at its literal strength: a limit by compactness establishes existence only together with proofs of the properties the problem names, and the problem names the mass gap and the axioms. Theorems 7.1–7.4 turn uniform clustering of the lattice correlations at a physical rate into the limit's gap and unique vacuum (Corollary 7.5: with (E0)–(E3) that is the mass gap and the axioms). Theorem 8.5 reduces that uniform clustering, for every limit point of a construction of the corpus's kind blocked at a fixed physical scale, to two finite statements about one block — Hypothesis I (the blocked measure's coarse variables satisfy Dobrushin's condition with an exponential weight) and Hypothesis II (the field inside a block clusters at the block scale). Theorem 8.7 proves the lattice gap at strong coupling on ℤ⁴ for β ≤ 0.241 on proved constants and on [0, 0.2452] on the exact ones, certified; Theorem 8.8 the same on ℤ³ for β ≤ 0.3739. The flux-surface gas (S1) carries the lattice gap toward β* ≈ 0.48 with exact non-abelian pricing, every number of it conditional tonight on three named items. The open link is the crossing: Hypothesis I at a fixed physical scale uniformly in the cutoff, from the strong-coupling region to asymptotic freedom's small-field region — the theorem Bałaban's program needs and never published (his Theorem 2, the sequence hypothesis's discharge), which is ours to prove.
