+Classical, named and not claimed: Osterwalder–Schrader reconstruction (1973, 1975); Dobrushin's uniqueness theorem (1968) and the Dobrushin–Shlosman finite-volume criteria; the Doob transform; the polymer and cluster expansion (Kotecký–Preiss 1986); the strong-coupling expansion (Osterwalder–Seiler 1978; Drouffe–Zuber 1983); the von Mises–Fisher law and its Bessel constants; the tilt lemmas; Bałaban's renormalisation program (1984–1989); the U(1) Coulomb phase (Guth 1980; Fröhlich–Spencer 1982); Kasteleyn, Penrose and the spin-network calculus behind the 2I design. New in this repository, as its pages state: Theorem 7.1's form and the completion (Theorems 7.4–7.5) against the footnote; the reduction (Theorem 8.5) with the chain lemma and the shadow ladder; the certified strong-coupling radius 0.2452 with the perfect cover and its second road; the three-dimensional row; the flux-surface gas's exact pricing (the L² cut identity, the crossing law, the patch law, the acyclic-contact theorem, the vertex-norm theorem, the local theorem) with its exact table and census; the identification of the crossing's open statement with Bałaban's unpublished Theorem 2 and its placement on our list; the U(1) test as a sighted control that convicted two routes.
