+| **W7 THE CONTINUUM LIMIT'S AXIOMS** | the existence of the limit per se (the corpus's Theorem 2.1 read to perfection or our own construction), OS0–OS4 on Schwinger distributions over ℝ⁴ⁿ, the Euclidean invariance of the limit, the identification (the step Theorem 10.8 of the corpus presupposes); the gap carried by Theorem 7.4 | the pages; the kernel where finite | a second seat; the kernel | an axiom failing for every limit point | after W6 |
