+**(p) THE PRIMITIVITY GAP AT THE DESK — THE SPHERE-SHEET CONJECTURE AS A STATEMENT ABOUT ONE MAP OF FREE GROUPS, AND THE BUDGET THAT CLOSES ITS SMALL CASES (2026-11-01 15:1x EST, read from `date`; the trunk seat; no run).** (1) THE MAP. Let X be Z₂-minimal with a sphere sheet Σ, P ⊂ Σ the contact preimage (connected, m faces), G the lattice contact graph; f: P → G the restriction of the sheet's map, two edges of P over every 4-link of G. The faces of P, based through a spanning tree, are a free basis of π₁(P) = F_{m−1} (the sphere is simply connected, the m face boundaries kill the free group of rank m − 1, and m − 1 elements that normally generate F_{m−1} form a basis), so the face words are the images of a basis under φ = f_*: π₁(P) → π₁(G) = F_r, and THEOREM S12-b's hypothesis holds iff φ EMBEDS π₁(P) ONTO A FREE FACTOR OF π₁(G). Minimality (CORRECTION (4)) is the mod-2 shadow: φ_*: H₁(P; Z₂) → H₁(G; Z₂) injective. THE CONJECTURE IS THEREFORE: for a minimal sphere-sheet set, the contact preimage's fundamental group embeds in the contact graph's as a free factor. (2) THE BUDGET. Each 4-link's two preimage edges lie on two face boundaries each (or on one boundary twice, as a bridge whose two traversals cancel in the reduced word), so for every chord x the reduced face words satisfy Σ_i |w_i|_x ≤ 4, with equality iff both preimage edges lie on cycles of P; and each preimage edge contributes x to one word and x⁻¹ to the other, so the exponent sum of x over all words is zero. (3) THE SMALL CASES CLOSED BY THE BUDGET. m = 2 (one cycle γ in P): words w, w⁻¹, and γ's nonzero Z₂-class gives a chord traversed exactly once — primitive (the one-cycle lemma). m = 3 with r = 2 (a theta graph over a figure-eight or a rectangle-with-diagonal): the words w₁, w₂, w₃ ≅ (w₁w₂)⁻¹ with Σ|w_i|_x ≤ 4 at each chord force |w₁|_x + |w₂|_x ≤ 2 + c_x (c_x the cancellations of x in w₁w₂); without cancellation the pair (w₁, w₂) is, up to inverses, (a, b) — a basis; with a cancellation the only shapes (a b with b⁻¹a⁻¹b; a b with b⁻¹a) have equal Z₂-classes and are not minimal. So every minimal sphere-sheet set with at most three faces over at most two independent contact cycles has primitive face words and reads S = 4 — the theta reading ½ → 4 of (6) is the general case here, not an instance. (4) WHAT REMAINS. For m ≥ 4 or r ≥ 3 the budget still bounds the words (total non-trivial length ≤ 4r over m − 1 words of independent Z₂-classes) but no argument yet makes the system primitive; a non-primitive system with independent mod-2 classes needs a word like a²b²a⁻¹b⁻¹ (primitive abelianisation, not primitive), which the budget forbids on two chords and permits in principle on more. The conjecture stands on exactly this: SHORT WORDS WITH INDEPENDENT CLASSES ARE PRIMITIVE SYSTEMS — a statement about free groups with a combinatorial budget, decidable case by case by Whitehead's algorithm on any object the enumerator produces, which is what the two-road reader will do when the Weingarten step is built (today it refuses r ≥ 2: 124 leaves to F = 26, every one read S ≤ 4 by the resolution road). The next instrument is that step; the next object a minimal sphere-sheet set with four faces, which no census has produced.
